From d63951958763062e56d8c69741b5a2d720beb892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:33:05 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op menu picture: a module tab may draw shapes, or show the
 game through a window and frame its camera

The optional export hos_coop_menu_picture (gpu/vk/hos_coop_menu_picture.h)
hands Hookshot's menu a list of coloured convex shapes, drawn in a square
over the top of the help column of a co-op module's tab, with the help box
under it. Version 2: the module may ask for the square `live`, a clear
window onto the game behind the menu (no dim there, a thin frame); Hookshot
tells it where the square is and the window's aspect.

The optional export hos_coop_view (host/hos_coop_view.h), asked in
hos_oot_free_view before the Debug tab's free camera, may replace the
gameplay camera's eye and target for a frame; the view is rebuilt from them
as the free camera's is.

The Multiplayer tab's Customize page shows the player's own Link in the
window, the camera turning around him, and a flat Link when there is none.
A module without the exports: no picture, the game's camera.
